  L('m2c5-3', 'm2c5', 'Applications of semi-supervised learning',
`Typical cases where labels are scarce:

• **Fraud and AML**: few confirmed cases, millions of transactions.
• **Credit risk**: **reject inference** — rejected applicants have no observed outcome; SSL can help infer their likely performance.
• **Document and text classification**: tagging contracts, news, complaints, ESG reports; only a sample is labelled by hand.
• **Speech and image recognition**, medical imaging.
• **Cyber security** and anomaly detection.
