  L('m2c7-3', 'm2c7', 'Batch, stochastic and mini-batch gradient descent; dynamic learning rates',
`• **Batch gradient descent**: gradient computed on the **whole** training set per update. Stable, smooth path, but slow and memory heavy for big data.
• **Stochastic gradient descent (SGD)**: update after **each single observation**. Fast, noisy updates; noise can help escape shallow local minima but the path zig-zags.
• **Mini-batch**: update on small batches (e.g. 32–256). The standard compromise; efficient on GPUs.
• An **epoch** = one full pass over the training data.

**Dynamic learning rates** improve convergence:
• **Schedules / decay**: start large, shrink over time (step decay, exponential decay).
• **Momentum**: add a fraction of the previous update to smooth oscillations and speed up.
• **Adaptive methods**: AdaGrad, RMSProp, **Adam** — per-parameter learning rates based on past gradients.`,
